2-id64" playOrder="90"><navLabel><text>Achieving Maximal Overlap in Practice</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_achieving_maximal_overlap_in_practice_1757308031865353"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="sect1-id65" playOrder="91"><navLabel><text>NVIDIA Magnum IO Optimization Stack</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nvidia_magnum_io_optimization_stack_1757308031865411"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect1-id66" playOrder="92"><navLabel><text>High-Speed, Low-Overhead Data Transfers with RDMA</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_high_speed_low_overhead_data_transfers_with_rdma_1757308031865485"/><navPoint id="sect2-id67" playOrder="93"><navLabel><text>Tuning Multinode Connectivity</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_tuning_multinode_connectivity_1757308031865542"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect2-id383" playOrder="94"><navLabel><text>Multinode Communication Pitfalls</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_multinode_communication_pitfalls_1757308031865599"/><navPoint id="sect3-id68" playOrder="95"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #1: Using a CPU-bound Gloo backend instead of NCCL</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_1_using_a_cpu_bound_gloo_backend_instead_1757308031865654"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id384" playOrder="96"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #2: Mismatched NCCL versions</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_2_mismatched_nccl_versions_1757308031865703"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id385" playOrder="97"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #3: TCP port exhaustion during NCCL bootstrap</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_3_tcp_port_exhaustion_during_nccl_bootst_1757308031865752"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id69" playOrder="98"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #4: Insufficient network bandwidth or misconfigured NICs</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_4_insufficient_network_bandwidth_or_misc_1757308031865800"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id386" playOrder="99"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #5: Straggler nodes or processes</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_5_straggler_nodes_or_processes_1757308031865847"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id70" playOrder="100"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #6: GPU memory fragmentation under UCX/RDMA</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_6_gpu_memory_fragmentation_under_ucx_rdm_1757308031865894"/></navPoint></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="sect1-id387" playOrder="101"><navLabel><text>NCCL for Distributed Multi-GPU Communication</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_for_distributed_multi_gpu_communication_1757308031865976"/><navPoint id="sect2-id71" playOrder="102"><navLabel><text>Topology Awareness in NCCL</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_topology_awareness_in_nccl_1757308031866050"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect2-id72" playOrder="103"><navLabel><text>NCCL Communication Algorithms</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_communication_algorithms_1757308031866097"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect2-id73" playOrder="104"><navLabel><text>Distributed Data Parallel Strategies</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_distributed_data_parallel_strategies_1757308031866147"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect2-id388" playOrder="105"><navLabel><text>NCCL Communicator Lifecycle and Environment Gotchas</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_communicator_lifecycle_and_environment_gotcha_1757308031866212"/><navPoint id="sect3-id74" playOrder="106"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #1: Creating NCCL communicators too often</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_1_creating_nccl_communicators_too_often_1757308031866274"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id462" playOrder="107"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #2: Do not create and destroy NCCL communicators on every iteration</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_2_do_not_create_and_destroy_nccl_communi_1757308031866325"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id75" playOrder="108"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #3: Avoid overtuning or disabling NCCL features with environment variables</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_3_avoid_overtuning_or_disabling_nccl_fea_1757308031866376"/><navPoint id="sect4-id76" playOrder="109"><navLabel><text>NCCL_NSOCKS_PERTHREAD and NCCL_SOCKET_NTHREADS (Socket/TCP transports)</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_nsocks_perthread_and_nccl_socket_nthreads_1757308031866429"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect4-id77" playOrder="110"><navLabel><text>NCCL_MIN_NCHANNELS and NCCL_MAX_NCHANNELS</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_min_nchannels_and_nccl_max_nchannels_1757308031866482"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect4-id78" playOrder="111"><navLabel><text>NCCL_TOPO_FILE</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_topo_file_1757308031866528"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect4-id715" playOrder="112"><navLabel><text>NCCL_MNNVL_ENABLE</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_sharp_enable_1757308031866579"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect4-id79" playOrder="113"><navLabel><text>NCCL_SHARP_DISABLE</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_nccl_sharp_disable_1757308031866579"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id80" playOrder="114"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #4: Verify CPU-GPU NUMA-node affinity for NCCL threads</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_4_verify_cpu_gpu_numa_node_affinity_for_1757308031866631"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id81" playOrder="115"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #5: Resist the temptation to ignore NCCL warnings and errors</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_5_resist_the_temptation_to_ignore_nccl_w_1757308031866681"/></navPoint><navPoint id="sect3-id82" playOrder="116"><navLabel><text>Pitfall #6: NCCL communicator hangs, errors, or shuts down completely</text></navLabel><content src="ch04.html#ch04_pitfall_6_nccl_communicator_hangs_errors_or_sh_1757308031866734"/></navPoint></navPoint><navPoint id="sect2-id83" playOrder="117"><navLabel><text>Profi